I did it.  I ascended.  O, O, O.  Watch me dance.

5365706  Jesse-Wiz-Elf-Fem-Cha ascended to demigoddess-hood.   210
[214]

Our hero was sent into the dungeons with a wand of fire, 2 potions of
holy water, a magic marker, and INT of 20.  I guess she had a troubled
childhood with the elves, because at the first shop she came to she
burned the owner alive and stole all his cash and items.  It was just
too tempting, a vast general store full of goodies, including
spellbooks, and poor elfy with only a few bucks in her torn pockets.

Having learned that crime pays very well in Nethack, elfy used the
remaining charges to kill the purveyor of an armor shop.  Now with
enough gold to buy protection, she made her way to minetown to find a
coaligned altar.  In this general store she noticed a lamp that cost 50
zorkmids, so she murdered the shopkeeper and stole the lamp, used the
holy water to bless it, and wished herself a SDSM.  Then, having
written a spellbook of magic missile by rinsing off a spellbook of
light, she proceeded to assasinate every shopkeeper in minetown save
Izchak and used their stolen livelihood toward divine protection.  Her
AC was now -8 and she hadn't gone beyond dungeon level 2 yet.

Mines, yawn, sokoban, yawn, back to mines with a potion of object
detection to grab a luckstone, yawn.  Wrote a spellbook of identify, SO
satisfying to drop all that worthless glass.  Then...wand of wishing
from a bones level.  Payback for all the times bones levels have caused
me to lose focus and crash, or stuck me with a polymorphed mind flayer.
 Soon I'm gliding through levels with speed boots and gauntlets of dex.


An altar on level 9 frustrated me until I was able to bring back a few
wands of create monster.  Finger of Death before Magicbane?  I would
later use the castle's wand of wishing to summon the delicious athame.

Two lepracaun halls in close succession.  By now elfy has fireball and
she's not afraid to use it, even if it's not as practical as FoD, it's
bloody great to imagine the meteors falling on the hapless little
creatures while they dream about lucky charms.

Elfy pauses at Medusa's level, having made it this far without a way to
cross the water.  She notices she has both polymorph and polymorph
control, however, so she turn into a silver dragon and flies across.
She lays three eggs before teleporting back to an elven form 3 levels
higher than previous!  Elfy now has a possy of mewing dragons that act
essentially as walking mirrors to her attack spells.  And now Perseus'
shattered statue ensures that she'll never have to leave her hot elf
body again.

The quest took about ten minutes.

The only other pause was at the Valley of the Dead.  The only other
time I'd made it this far I got poisoned by Jubilex with no way to cure
myself.  And elfy has no way to cure herself now.  So it's back up to
the dungeon to sacrifice and pray and scour, and soon I'm sitting
pretty with a cure sickness spell.  By now elfy is casting magic
mapping at 0% fail and so I take a moment to clear out Fort Ludios,
surprised that I can kill so many and not see my hero advance in level
any more.

Gehennom was fast.  At one point I lost the three levels of experience
to a sneaky Vampire while dancing with a nurse, but I gained these
levels back in exactly the same way as before, first polymorphing into
a rock mole, eating three rings of gain constitution, then back to
elf...kind of like in "The Fly" how teleporting yourself was supposed
to clean you of impurities of whatever.

I paused before knocking on Rodney's door to write an anxious message
on this board about fighting Death. Elfy stockpiled at level 1, using
the Eye to hop around.  Rodney's a stupid little punk, isn't he?  FoD
in your face again and again.

Elfy should not have survived Endgame.  Her unicorn horn was not
blessed.  She had only one holy water - just lazy, no other word for
it.  Only one wand of death.  Only one wand of teleport.  No way of
finding the portals except for a single charge on her crystal ball to
help her get through Earth.  Most of all, she wasn't prepared for the
effect on spellcasting that holding the amulet would have.  And MOST of
all she wasn't prepared for the fury of the archon.  Soon elfy was a
blind, confused mess, and all the mind flayers that the stupid archons
had summoned had made her forget what half her inventory was.

A little more effort right before the endgame probably could have
scrounged up another wish for a magic marker, and I could have
genocided all mind flayers and all liches, and I could have had a lot
of holy water, and a LAMP or any kind of light source to help me
thorugh the fire level!

But it didn't matter - Elfy DID have a ring of conflict, and that was
really all it took.  Pestilence and famine fell victim to Elfy's
spellcasting and Death proved to be a softie.  The third altar was
coaligned; I did not hesitate.

I have so many to thank - the kind people of this board, the company I
work for for PAYING me while I do this (usually it's just a post-lunch
malaise thing, but the last few days...forget it, it's been non-stop),
my girlfriend for letting me read spoilers while she watches So You
Think You Can Dance...it's been great, and I'm sure I'll be back soon,
probably as a monk.

Peace!



